{
  "_header": [
    "th#1871 P1 / pgw#1225 — POSTURE WIRE CONFORMANCE VECTORS.",
    "Vendored BYTE-IDENTICALLY in tensorhub (internal/orchestrator/measurement/testdata/) and",
    "python-gen-worker (tests/testdata/). scripts/posture-vector-drift.sh gates it, PGW LANDS FIRST.",
    "",
    "WHAT EACH SIDE OWES THIS FILE, and why neither half is the property alone:",
    "  python-gen-worker  every `wire` object is exactly what the SDK's own posture serializes to",
    "                     (gen_worker.measured_posture.wire_json). It proves the PRODUCER's shape.",
    "  tensorhub          every `wire` object decodes to measurement.Posture and digests to",
    "                     `posture_digest`, with the stated `degraded` / `posture_mismatches` /",
    "                     `applied_techniques` renderings. It proves the CONSUMER's identity.",
    "",
    "THE DIGEST HAS EXACTLY ONE IMPLEMENTATION and it is tensorhub's. The worker never computes",
    "one — a second canonicalization of the same object is two implementations free to disagree",
    "while both suites stay green, which is pgw#1188's topology divergence one contract over.",
    "So the digests below are OPAQUE to python-gen-worker: it pins them, it does not derive them.",
    "",
    "`identity_rules` is the part that can go red for a REASON. Each row names two vectors and",
    "whether they are the same measurement. Those are DESIGN-RULINGS §1.36 decisions, not",
    "implementation details, and a change that flips one is a change to what the platform",
    "believes a measurement is."
  ],
